# RETURN in a function block and in a function.
#
# Derivation (ed.3 7.3.3.3.4 / ed.2 3.3.2.3: RETURN "provides early exit
# from a function, function block or program"):
#   GUARD: calls is incremented before the test, so it counts every
#   invocation; y is only written when x >= 0 and keeps its last value
#   otherwise (FB outputs are retained between calls).
#   CLAMP10: v <= 10 gives v + 100; v > 10 returns 10 before the + 100.
# cycle 0: x=3  -> y=6,  calls=1, c=103
# cycle 1: x=-1 -> RETURN before y: y=6 kept, calls=2, c=99
# cycle 2: x=15 -> y=30, calls=3, c=10 (returned before + 100)
# cycle 3: x=0  -> y=0,  calls=4, c=100
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: x
outputs: y calls c
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 7.3.3.3.4 (RETURN), 6.6.3.1 (FB outputs retained); ed.2 3.3.2.3
---
0 x=3 => y=6 calls=1 c=103
1 x=-1 => y=6 calls=2 c=99
2 x=15 => y=30 calls=3 c=10
3 x=0 => y=0 calls=4 c=100
